# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# cg_shift_demo.fd
#
# Fault scenario: forward CG shift equal to the CG-CB vertical separation.
#
# Background: the Odyssey is trimmed with vs_zg = 0.082 m (CG below the
# centerline) and vs_zb = 0.0 m (CB on centerline), giving a vertical
# CG-CB separation of 0.082 m.  This separation provides roll restoring
# moment.  Shifting vs_xg forward by the same 0.082 m represents a
# realistic mass redistribution (e.g. a shifted battery pack) and
# introduces a significant pitch-down moment that the elevator must work
# to counteract.
#
# Trigger: vehicle reaches 5 m depth (m_depth > 5.0).
# Action:  vs_xg = 0.082  (forward of the nominal 0.0 m)
#
# The fault is persistent -- it remains active every cycle once triggered.
# To model a one-time step change that stays, this is correct behavior.
#
# Expected observable effect: increased nose-down pitch tendency, elevator
# deflection increase, possible depth excursion if PID gains are marginal.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

fault: m_depth > 5.0 -> vs_xg = 0.082
